---
import PageLayout from '../../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import LegalIdentity from '../../components/LegalIdentity.astro';
import { route } from '../../i18n/routes';
import { AUTHOR_NAME, AUTHOR_DESC, CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../../data/site-config';
import { VALUE } from '../../content/home';
import { KIT as K } from '../../lib/kit';
import { profilePageSchema, breadcrumbSchema } from '../../lib/seo';
const lang = 'en';
const path = route('about', lang);
const title = 'Travel Vaccines by Country 2026: Who Publishes This Site';
const description = `Travel vaccines by country, published by Radif Partners from CDC pages for ${K.dests.length} destinations and public price lists: no clinic, no booking, no form, no fee.`;
---
<PageLayout title={title} description={description} lang={lang} jsonLd={[profilePageSchema({ path, lang }), breadcrumbSchema([{ name: 'Home', path: route('home', lang) }, { name: 'About', path }])]} breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'About' }]}>
  <article class="prose prose-slate max-w-none prose-headings:font-serif">
    <h1>About Vaccines by Country</h1>
    <p>{AUTHOR_DESC.en}</p>
    <h2>Why this site exists</h2>
    <p>Preparing a trip means reading one CDC page per country, then the entry rules of each border, then guessing how early to start and what it will cost. The pages that explain vaccines rarely do the arithmetic, and the clinics that do it rarely publish a price before an appointment. This site puts the steps together for a whole route.</p>
    <p>{VALUE}</p>
    <h2>Who publishes it</h2>
    <p>The site is published by {AUTHOR_NAME}, a company that builds calculators on public rules and public data. It is not a clinic, a pharmacy, a travel agency or a health authority, and it is not affiliated with or endorsed by CDC, the US government, the NHS or any health department. It sells no vaccine, books no appointment, sends no lead to anyone, receives no commission and carries no affiliate link.</p>
    <LegalIdentity lang={lang} />
    <h2>What we rely on</h2>
    <p>The CDC Travelers' Health page of each of {K.num(K.dests.length)} destinations, read on {K.day(K.CDC_DATE)}, quoted with attribution and without change to its substance as CDC's conditions of reuse require; the material is available free of charge on cdc.gov. The CDC Yellow Book for schedules and contraindications. The self-pay price lists of {K.num(K.fees.length)} US county health departments, each with its link and date; the CDC adult vaccine price list of {K.day(K.priceList.list_date)}; the NADAC survey of pharmacy drug costs of {K.day(K.NADAC_DATE)}; and the NHS travel vaccinations page for UK travelers.</p>
    <h2>What the site leaves out</h2>
    <p>Prices at private travel clinics and pharmacies, which are not published with a date; UK, Canadian and Australian prices for the same reason; the WHO country list, whose licence does not allow commercial reuse; and any personal advice. Pregnancy, a weakened immune system, allergies and children's schedules are for a clinician. The <a href={route('method', lang)}>method page</a> lists every source and limit; the <a href={route('editorial', lang)}>editorial policy</a> explains corrections.</p>
    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>, for corrections, a price list we missed or a rule that changed. We answer questions about a figure or a source, not about your own health or trip: for that, a doctor, nurse or pharmacist is the right person.</p>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
